Hi,

I agree with your motivations from the point of view of maintaining
TeX, minimising confusion, classifying packages etc.  But, forgetting
history for a moment (!), consider things from the user's point of
view---particularly that of a new user.  There is a big enough
proliferation of terminology without having to learn that the logical
and likely-sounding style option 'times' should be referred to as
'nftimes'.  Unfortunately, I can't say that I see any way around this.
Perhaps the compatibility files that you mention could, by default
say "Didn't you intend nftimes here?".

Just a small point from the viewpoint of trying to make LaTeX less
hostile to the novice.

Gavin

